stays open under that LICENSE.

1. WHOSE IT IS
   This software is mine. Every file, every line, every migration, the
   Durable Objects, the pages, the seed data, the docs. Reading it is fine.
   Learning from it is fine. Taking it is not.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO
   a. Read the source and run it on your own machine to evaluate it.
   b. Use the hosted Qollab that QNTBR runs, under the terms of that service.
   c. Build your own accounts, rooms or parties for your own game, from your
      own code. The open client in packages/util is yours to use for that.
   d. Send fixes back. A contribution you send is licensed to QNTBR without
      restriction, so it can ship.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO (without a written license from QNTBR)
   a. Copy, fork, redistribute, sublicense or sell this software or a
      substantial part of it.
   b. Run it, or a copy of it, as a service for anyone other than yourself,
      including the players of your own game.
   c. Strip this notice, the name Qollab or the QNTBR mark from it.
   d. Train a model on it to reproduce it.

4. YOUR DATA IS YOURS
   Nothing here gives QNTBR any right to the data you or your players put
   into Qollab beyond what it takes to run the service. Accounts, saves,
   friends and messages stay theirs, and the software is built so every row
   can be exported and deleted.

